  "id": "associated-movement",
  "term": "associated movement",
  "definition": "In this historical usage, associated movement means the pupil’s contraction that normally occurs along with focusing on a near object and converging the eyes. The passage contrasts this associated pupillary action with the light reflex, noting that one may be preserved when the other is lost.",
